## SDK Reference

**Get SDK Instance**

Account calls work only in a plugin's pages; the Prelude script (`index.js`) cannot reach them. `accountSDK` is a singleton: give it the page's channel before using it.

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="ts"}
---
code: |
  import { accountSDK } from '@talex-touch/utils'
  import { useChannel } from '@talex-touch/utils/plugin/sdk'

  accountSDK.setChannelSend(useChannel().send)
  await accountSDK.getProfile()
---
:::

A plugin uses these methods, opening the sign-in and account pages included, only after it declares `account.read` in `manifest.json` and the user grants it. Without the grant, `usePluginAccount()` calls reject with `ACCOUNT_PERMISSION_DENIED` and `onDidChange` never calls back; `accountSDK` reads its queries as "none", and its page openers reject. See [Permission System](./permission.en.mdc).

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="json"}
---
code: |
  {
    "permissions": {
      "required": ["account.read"]
    },
    "permissionReasons": {
      "account.read": "Shows your plan and the quota you have left"
    }
  }
---
:::

::alert{type="warning"}
**Note**: `accountSDK` reads a failed call as "none": `getProfile()` returns `null` and `isLoggedIn()` returns `false`. To tell signing out from a failed call, or to hear when the sign-in changes, use `usePluginAccount()` below.
::

---

**Following the Sign-in**

`usePluginAccount()` is the account client for plugin pages. Its calls reject when they fail instead of reading as signed out, and `onDidChange` tells the plugin when the sign-in changes.

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="ts"}
---
code: |
  import { usePluginAccount } from '@talex-touch/utils/plugin/sdk'

  const account = usePluginAccount()

  const stop = account.onDidChange((session) => {
    // The stored sign-in has not been checked in this run yet, so "signed out" may still turn signed in
    if (!session.isSettled)
      return
    renderUser(session.user) // null when signed out
  })

  // When the page unmounts
  stop()
---
:::

| Method | Return | Description |
|--------|--------|-------------|
| `getProfile()` | `UserProfile \| null` | The signed-in account's profile, `null` when signed out |
| `getSubscription()` | `Subscription \| null` | Subscription |
| `getUsage()` | `UsageStats \| null` | Usage |
| `getFeatures()` | `FeatureFlag[]` | The plan's features: `aiRequests` and `aiTokens` carry their limit in `value` (`-1` for unlimited); `customModels`, `prioritySupport` and `apiAccess` are on or off |
| `getTeams()` | `Team[]` | The organization the account belongs to, empty when there is none; the personal team is not listed |
| `openUpgradePage(plan?)` | `void` | Opens the pricing page in the browser, with `plan` outlined when given |
| `openBillingPage()` | `void` | Opens the team page, where the plan and activation codes are managed |
| `openAccountSettings()`, `openProfileEditor()` | `void` | Opens the account page |
| `requestLogin()` | `boolean` | Joins the sign-in when the app is signed in or a sign-in is under way, and opens the sign-in page otherwise. `true` does not mean anyone is signed in yet; `false` means the page could not be opened |
| `onDidChange(callback)` | `() => void` | Calls back once with the current state, then after every change; returns a function that stops it |

The state `onDidChange` receives (`AccountSessionState`):

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `isSettled` | `boolean` | The stored sign-in has been checked in this run. While `false`, signed out does not mean the account signed out |
| `isSignedIn` | `boolean` | Signed in |
| `user` | `{ id: string, name?: string } \| null` | The signed-in account, `null` when signed out |

The state carries no credential and no email, and a change to details it does not carry does not call back.

